title: LSP Document Highlight - (Example)

\procedure lsp.dh.greet(who) Hello <<who>> {{{ [<who>] }}}
\procedure lsp.dh.outer(lsp.dh.greet) <<lsp.dh.greet>>

<<lsp.dh.greet who:"World">> <<lsp.dh.greet>>

<$let who="you"><<who>></$let>

Open this tiddler's `.tid` file in your editor and put the cursor on each name.

|! Cursor on |! Lights up |
|`who` in the body of `lsp.dh.greet` |its declaration in the head and both uses in that body, nothing else |
|`who` inside the `$let` |the `$let`'s `who` and the use inside it |
|`lsp.dh.greet` in the first call |the definition's name and both calls on that line, not the call inside `lsp.dh.outer`, where a parameter of that name hides it |

